wiretap-server (0.1.1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Taps a Modbus RTU line read-only through a [[device]] table, into a
    gateway database of its own. The unit now allows USB serial adapters,
    read-only, and runs the daemon with the dialout group.
  * Speaks ingest protocol v2. Upgrade the gateway before this package: a
    0.1.1 gateway still accepts a 0.1.0 daemon, but a 0.1.1 daemon is
    refused by a 0.1.0 gateway and caches to disk until it is upgraded.
  * A config file naming neither [server] iface nor a [[device]] now
    captures nothing. Every file this package has written names iface.

 -- Alex Ferrara <alex@wiredsquare.com>  Fri, 12 Sep 2026 07:40:00 +0930

wiretap-server (0.1.0) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * First packaged release; the Python it replaces had no packaging at all.
  * Pre-1.0: the interfaces are not stable and the ingest wire format is
    expected to break at v2. Pin exactly.
  * Upgrading from a Python deployment: its unit at
    /etc/systemd/system/wiretap-server.service is stopped and moved aside to
    .pre-deb, because it shares this package's unit name and /etc outranks
    /usr/lib. The new daemon is deliberately not started - carry the settings
    across first. Its disk cache is moved to /var/lib/wiretap-server/ for the
    daemon to adopt, since the unit's ProtectHome= hides the old location.
  * The daemon runs as the system user `wiretap`, not as `pi`.

 -- Alex Ferrara <alex@wiredsquare.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +1000
